    "result_text": "The full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the customerCode de-duplication rule: when a computed `customerCode` collides with an existing owner's code, `-<n>` is appended with the smallest `n \u2265 2` that makes it unique.\n\n**Where the logic lives** \u2014 I kept concerns separated following the repo's existing idiom (small single-responsibility collaborators like `CityOwnerCounter`/`NamesakeCounter` that query `ClinicService`):\n\n- **New `CustomerCodeDeduplicator`** (`rest/validation/`) \u2014 a `@Component` that takes a candidate code and returns a de-duplicated one. It collects existing owners' customer codes into a set and, on collision, probes `candidate-2`, `candidate-3`, \u2026 until it finds an unused suffix. `CustomerCodeGenerator` stays focused purely on deriving the base `<REGION>-<HASH8>` code.\n\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1`** \u2014 injected the new component and, in `addOwner`, generate the base code then pass it through `customerCodeDeduplicator.deduplicate(...)` before setting it on the owner. Because the membership number is derived from `customerCode` afterward, it correctly picks up the de-duplicated value.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreCustomerCodesStayUnique` (distinct owners always get distinct codes) passes, and the rest of the suite remains green.",
